  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved the best validation accuracy (0.591) so far, a substantial +0.106 improvement over singleprofile RNA (config_001, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is beneficial. However, we have only tested one aggregation method (avgpool). Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform simple average pooling for combining multiple RNA profiles? This experiment (config_003) isolates exactly that variable—same model setting, same profile setting, same RNA encoder, only aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer. Why best next step: It is a clean single-variable comparison extending our strongest result, directly informing whether the added complexity of a transformer aggregator is warranted before we invest budget in multimodal configurations where aggregation design will be even more critical. A positive result would justify transformer in multimodal settings; a null or negative result would steer us toward simpler, more robust aggregation strategies."
}

